{#-
  The index of every world, written once and shown after <main> on every page but the two that
  list every page themselves (sitemap.html, moods.html). It is the one list of worlds the site
  has, and _data/worlds.json is the one place the list and every world's name are kept: a world
  is added, renamed or retired there, and this include, the header, sitemap.html and the sky
  circuit all follow.

  Two groups, in the words every page uses: off the sky (six worlds that share nothing but the
  site) and under the sky (eight that read one saved sky). Under each name is the orientation the
  world answers to, which is the same phrase the ribbon reads a visitor as. On a world under the
  sky that group comes first and carries the circuit: which of the eight this is, and the next.

  The headings are real (h2, then h3), so a visitor listening to the page hears its shape, and the
  reachability axiom holds with scripting off because every link here is plain markup. One
  button, "send me somewhere", is the site's one way of being sent at random (js/site.js).
-#}
{%- set here = (page.filePathStem | replace('/', '')) + '.html' if page else '' -%}
{%- set skyIndex = -1 -%}
{%- for world in worlds.underSky %}{% if world.file == here %}{% set skyIndex = loop.index0 %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set groups = [['sky', 'under the sky', worlds.underSky], ['off', 'off the sky', worlds.offSky]] if skyIndex >= 0 else [['off', 'off the sky', worlds.offSky], ['sky', 'under the sky', worlds.underSky]] -%}
<footer class='site-footer'>
  <nav class='panel worlds' aria-labelledby='worlds-title'>
    <h2 class='panel-title' id='worlds-title'>every world</h2>
    <p class='panel-note'>Fourteen worlds and no default. Under each name is who the site would send there: take the one that fits, or the one that does not.</p>
{%- for group in groups %}
    <section class='worlds-group' aria-labelledby='worlds-{{ group[0] }}'>
      <h3 class='panel-label' id='worlds-{{ group[0] }}'>{{ group[1] }}</h3>
{%- if group[0] == 'sky' %}
{%- if skyIndex >= 0 %}
{%- set nextWorld = worlds.underSky[(skyIndex + 1) % worlds.underSky.length] %}
      <p class='panel-note'>These eight read one saved sky, the stars placed in the wish constellation. This is {{ skyIndex + 1 }} of 8. <a href='{{ siteRoot }}{{ nextWorld.file }}'>next: {{ nextWorld.name }}</a></p>
{%- else %}
      <p class='panel-note'>These eight read one saved sky; the wish constellation is where it is placed.</p>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
      <ul class='chips chips-tall'>
{%- for world in group[2] %}
        <li><a href='{{ siteRoot }}{{ world.file }}'{% if world.file == here %} class='current' aria-current='page'{% endif %}>{{ world.name }}<span>{{ world.orientation }}</span></a></li>
{%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
{%- endfor %}
    <p class='panel-foot'>
      <button type='button' id='worlds-random' hidden>send me somewhere</button>
      <span>Or <a href='{{ siteRoot }}sitemap.html'>site map</a> for every page with a line on what it is.</span>
    </p>
  </nav>
</footer>
